-- title:
--   Igusa branch rings stay distinct on the level field
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Two function fields are in play: $\bar F =$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, and the characteristic-$q$ field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, generated over the residue field of $A$ by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC`.
--
--   Reduction data. `W` is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A`, and `hW` says that its members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those places that are rational, are affine geometric places, and send the geometric $j$-generator into `ssJSet q`, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves have no nonzero $q$-torsion point. `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base-changed full-level-$M'$ modular function field into $\bar F$. `R₀` is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, i.e. a valuation subring `R₀.integers` with surjective residue map onto the characteristic-$q$ field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ on constants, satisfying the scaling condition `exists_smul_mem`, and equipped with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors. `hR₀` states the coefficientwise compatibility: if $y$ is a Laurent series over $A$ whose image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, then that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Branch rings. `ζ : Idx q` is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `OIg` assigns a valuation subring of $\bar F$ to each point of $\mathbf P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, and `OSS` assigns one to each member of `W`. The hypotheses on `OIg` are: `hIg_inf`, which identifies the ring at `lineInfty q` as the Gauss ring, $f$ lying in it exactly when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`; `hIg`, which provides for each line $\ell$ some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and `OIg ℓ` equal to the pullback of the Gauss ring along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of `OIg`; and `hIg_perm`, which says that for every `ζ' : Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family `OIg`. The hypotheses on `OSS` are: `hSS_A`, that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `OSS s` exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` having non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the base-changed $j$-expansion `jq` has non-negative order, and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, asserts that the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in `OSS s` and that for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of the residue of $f$ at $s$ the difference $f - a$ lies in the maximal ideal of `OSS s`; `hSS_fix`, the invariance of each `OSS s` under pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, the existence for each $s$ of a transversal parameter $t \in$ `OSS s` such that $t - a$ is a unit of `OSS s` for every $a \in A$.
--
--   Prolongation and constants. `R` is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\bar F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` — a valuation subring with surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing the residue map of $A$ on constants and satisfying `exists_smul_mem` — and `hR` identifies `R.integers` with the Gauss ring `OIg (lineInfty q)`; `hR₀O` says that $f$ lies in `R₀.integers` precisely when its image in $\bar F$ lies in the Gauss ring. Further, $\pi \in A$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$. A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\mathbb Q$ is given together with $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$, and the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` states that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. Auxiliary level data: a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ with $A_1 = A \cap K_1$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   Conclusion. With $\bar F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\bar F$ over $k_0$ subject to four conditions: the constants together with $F_0$ generate $\bar F$, that is `adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M'))) ⊔ F₀ = ⊤`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of $T(K') =$ `adjoin k₀ (image of K' in fieldBar) ⊔ F₀` with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, all $a_i$ vanish; and that every element of $\bar F$ whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1 =$ `adjoin k₀ (image of K₁ in fieldBar) ⊔ F₀` for the resulting level field. The assertion is made for any $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees on $A_1 \subseteq K_1$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, and for any $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $\bar F$ is the element `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` applied to the class of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`, with $j_1 \ne 0$.
--
--   Six auxiliary predicates on the two-chart integral model $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures `chartAlgFin`, `chartAlgInf` of $A_1[j_1]$, $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$ in $T_1$) are then introduced as local abbreviations: `InStalk x f`, that $f$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h$ in the relevant chart algebra and $h$ outside the prime of any chart point above $x$; `InMax x f`, the same with $g$ moreover inside that prime; `Centred P x`, that a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is rational and that for every $f$ in the stalk at $x$ one has $f \in P$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ exactly when `InMax x f`; `GoodPt x`, that $x$ maps to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$, specialises only to itself, that every chart element whose image lies in the non-units of `R.integers` lies in the prime of each chart point above $x$, and that for each point of the finite chart above $x$ and each homomorphism $\varphi$ of `chartAlgFin` onto an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with kernel that prime, $\varphi(j_1) \notin$ `ssJSet q`; `Reads x Q`, that every $f$ in the stalk at $x$ lies in `R.integers` with `R.residue f` in the valuation subring of a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, a non-unit there exactly when `InMax x f`; and `OffBranch x`, that for every line other than `lineInfty q` and every chart point above $x$ some chart element whose image lies in the non-units of the corresponding `OIg` avoids that prime. These abbreviations do not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   The conclusion is the injectivity of the Igusa branch rings after restriction to $T_1$: for all points $\ell, \ell'$ of $\mathbf P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ (the binder names reuse the name of the auxiliary prime above), if for every $f \in T_1$ the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in `OIg ℓ` if and only if it lies in `OIg ℓ'`, then $\ell = \ell'$.
--
--   The Igusa branch rings of the geometric full-level field are pairwise distinct by hypothesis `hIg_inj`; this statement says that they remain pairwise distinct when tested only on the level field $T_1 = K_1 \cdot F_0$, which is what makes the branches of the two-chart integral model over $A_1$ separate. It is used in the construction of the model, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_igusaRing_coe_levelField_and_injective_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_igusaRing_coe_levelField_and_injective_twoChartIntegralModel), and rests on the uniqueness of the prolongation of a valuation along the constant extension together with the Gauss-ring description of the branch at infinity.
